  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "In a carnot engine, the temperature of reservoir is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>527</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and that of sink&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. If the workdone by the engine when it transfers heat from reservoir&nbsp;to sink is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi></math>, the quantity of heat absorbed by the engine from reservoir is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "16",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Efficiency of Carnot engine is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>Q</mi></mfrac></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is heat absorbed.</p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>527</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mn>800</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mi>Q</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12000</mn><mi>Q</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>",
